    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d137">

                <pb facs="0217" n="205" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg205"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">847.24/775</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Australian Minister for External Affairs</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Evatt</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the American Minister in Australia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)<anchor n="51"
                        xml:id="d137-f1"/>
                </head>
                <p>The Minister of State for External Affairs presents his compliments to the
                    Honourable the American Minister, and has the honour to acknowledge the receipt
                    of his communication of December 23rd last and subsequent memorandum<anchor
                        n="52" xml:id="d137-f2"/> regarding the proposal of the Government of the
                    United States of America, first communicated to the Australian Government on 6th
                    October, 1943,<anchor n="53" xml:id="d137-f3"/> in relation to bringing under
                    the reverse lend-lease system those materials which are imported from Australia
                    or from Australian sources by agencies of the United States Government.</p>
                <p>The proposal of the United States Government has been again fully considered by
                    the Australian Government in the light of the further circumstances adduced in
                    the communications above referred to, for which the Australian Government is
                    grateful.</p>
                <p>However, all the resources of this country have been and still are strained to
                    the utmost limit, and the Australian Government is therefore compelled to adhere
                    to the decision previously reached and communicated to the State Department on
                    5th November last.<anchor n="53" xml:id="d137-f4"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Canberra</hi>
                        </placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-28">28 January,
                            1944</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d137-f1" n="51" type="source" xml:id="d137-f1-content">
